//? Title: Multiclass structured-SVM special case: actual SGD and decision regions
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A linear multiclass hinge model separates three two-feature Gaussian clusters.
This Crammer-Singer special case exposes actual sampled subgradient updates,
full-data epoch diagnostics, decision regions and independently seeded held-out
predictions.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For augmented x=(features,1), scores are w_c*x. Minimize
lambda/2*sum_c||w_c||^2 + mean_i[max_c(w_c*x_i+[c!=y_i])-w_y*x_i]. Bias
coefficients are regularized. At update t choose a training row with replacement
and the lowest-index loss-augmented maximizing class before shrink. With
eta=1/(lambda*t), shrink every coefficient by1-eta*lambda; if the maximizing
class differs from truth, add eta*x to the true row and subtract it from the
selected row. There is no Pegasos projection. Each epoch performs n independent
draws, not a shuffle. The objective may fluctuate. This implementation is linear
multiclass classification, not general sequence/tree structured inference or a
kernel solver.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/structured_svm_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/structured_svm_analysis.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::StructuredSVMParameters p;
    p.lambda = 1;
    p.epochs = 2;
    p.seed = 1;
    auto r = a::structured_svm_trace({{1, 0}, {0, 1}}, {0, 1}, 2, p);
    std::print("| actual t | sampled row | truth | violator | rate | shrink | actual weights after |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | `{}` |\n",
                   s.iteration, s.example, s.truth, s.violator, s.rate,
                   s.shrink, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Two actual labelled feature rows");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} sampled SGD updates", r.updates));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Final objective {:.4g}",
                                     r.epochs.back().objective.value));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/structured_svm_tiny.svg");
}
```
